# <%= name %>

A SvelteKit application using Canonical styles<% if (appShell) { %> and application layouts<% } %>.
Use `summon domain billing --framework svelte`, `summon page billing/detail
--framework svelte`, and `summon wrapper settings --framework svelte` for
SvelteKit routes and wrappers.

Run `bun install`, `bun run check`, `bun run build`, `bun run test`, and `bun run dev`.
Commit the resulting lockfile and use `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI;
without a lockfile, transitive dependencies can change between installs.
Run `bun run storybook` or `bun run build:storybook` for the example stories.
<% if (forms) { %>After installing a Playwright Chromium browser, run `bun run test:browser`
against the built app to check contact error isolation and draft preservation<% if (appShell) { %>,
instance flows, heading focus and settings confirmation<% } %>.
Set `CHROMIUM_PATH` to use an existing Chromium executable.
<% } %>
The catalog uses local sample data. GraphQL and Relay are not included.
<% if (spa) { %>
This client-only application builds to `build/`. Configure the static host to
serve `200.html` as the fallback for application routes. Cold requests do not
receive server-rendered content or route-specific HTTP statuses.
Theme, dashboard settings and demo instances use local browser storage; there are no server
actions; the demo account session uses sessionStorage and is not authentication.
<% } else { %>
The production server is built with adapter-node; start it with `bun run preview`.
Configure `HOST`, `PORT` and `ORIGIN` for deployment.
Theme and locale are selected per request, and the sitemap is served at
`/sitemap.xml`. The dashboard's demo cookie is not authentication.<% if (appShell && forms) { %>
Instances are bounded browser-cookie demonstrations, not provisioned resources.
Removal uses a separate confirmation page without JavaScript and a hydrated modal.<% } %>
<% } %>
<% if (appShell) { %>
Pathname navigation focuses the new page heading; query-only navigation keeps Kit's
normal focus behavior. The settings project confirmation is a demonstration and
does not delete data. The dashboard navigation and instance creation panel use
native disclosures<% if (forms) { %>; when hydrated, the creation panel opens as a side sheet<% } %>.
<% } %>
